invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide.c
catches: diff_x25519_wide
reason: the ladder swaps the points once a step, by the step's bit exclusive-or
  the bit before, so after the last step the points stay swapped when bit 0
  is 1, and a cswap by bit 0 undoes that. A clamped scalar's bit 0 is 0, so
  x25519_wide() and every vector run right without it. bin/diff_x25519_wide
  runs x25519_wide_ladder on scalars that no clamp has touched against the
  Lean ladder, and about half of them set bit 0 (docs/decisions.md 152).

--- old
    cswap(a, b, bit);
    cswap(c, d, bit);
    invert(c, c);
--- new
    invert(c, c);
